OL,3,GNEWSAShop owners upbeat despite
OL,4,A'devastating' break-in
OL,5,
OL,6,FA shop owner has said she felt like
OL,7,Fclosing down for good after a break-in,
OL,8,Fbut the "amazing" community response
OL,9,Freminded her why it was still worth
OL,10,Fstaying open.
OL,12,FThe front door of Mansfield Shoe
OL,13,FRepairs, in Nottinghamshire, was
OL,14,Fsmashed early on Tuesday morning before
OL,15,Fhundreds of pounds worth of stock was
OL,16,Ftaken.
OL,18,FCarey Robertson, who runs the business
OL,19,Fwith her husband Scott, said the
OL,20,F"devastation" of seeing the break-in
OL,21,Fleft her feeling this might be the time
OL,22,Fto close after 23 years.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
